In article <19069@pasteur.Berkeley.EDU> kemnitz@postgres.Berkeley.EDU (Greg Kemnitz) writes:
>Polymorph
>
>Wands of polymorph should be used on piles of items.  When one has a wand
>of polymorph, one should stack armor, weapons, food, gems, etc in a huge
>pile (possibly the collected stuff of several levels).  

You can use more than one pile, which makes picking the objects out of them
easier.  Up to 5 piles in a line can be used, although the stuff in the 5th
pile does not always get polymorphed.

If you still have your dog, you can polymorph it in addition to the piles of
stuff until you get something nice.  As an aside, my experiments with rings of
conflict indicate that a guardian naga can kill every other monster, even
Demogorgons :-).


>Once armor is blessed, enchant armor will only add +1 to it - if it is cursed
>or normal, enchant armor will add +3 to it.

Not true.  The number of plusses a blessed scroll of enchant armor will add is
random, and appears to depend on the number of plusses the item already has,
not on whether it is cursed or blessed.


>Wands:
>
>1. Wand of wishing (Can be wished for, but uncharged - get scroll of charging)

This doesn't work.  Wands of wishing can only by charged once, and wished-for
wands of wishing have already been charged (and have no charges left).


>A Suggested Order for Wishing:
>
>1.  blessed +3 broadsword named Stormbringer
>2.  uncursed +3 orange dragon scale mail
>3.  uncursed +3 gauntlets of power
>4.  uncursed +3 shield of reflection
>5.  uncursed +3 speed boots
>6.  blessed tinning kit
>7.  blessed luckstone
>8.  3 blessed scrolls of enchant armor

I prefer the following:

1. blessed +3 speed boots
	The most important item in the game.  Most monsters can be killed
	without them getting a single hit on you.  The exceptions are
	missile-throwers and fast monsters such as leocrottas.
2. blessed +3 grey dragon scale mail
	Gives magic resistance.
3. a blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir
	A truly stupendous weapon (except against lightning resistant monsters,
	notably iron golems, black puddings and blue dragons).
